      "side": 1,
      "message": "The naming of `encode_dict_value` is a little inaccurate, when it specifically means \"encode anything other than a dict\" (and is used as such). I also don\u0027t think we get much value from separating list encoding from primitive encoding. How about you restructure this as such?:\n\n```\ndef json_encode(input):\n  def encode_shallow_value(v):\n    if type(input) \u003d\u003d \"list\":\n      ...\n    elif type(input) \u003d\u003d \"string\":\n      ...\n    else:\n      fail(...)\n\n\n  if type(input) \u003d\u003d \"dict\":\n    items \u003d []\n    for (k, v) in input.items():\n      if type(v) \u003d\u003d \"dict\":\n        fail(...)\n      else:\n        items +\u003d [encode_shallow_value(v) + ...]\n  else:\n    return encode_shallow_value(input)\n```",
      "revId": "1a1137d6aa1c447e35d3a0ee896c3275239f6225",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "fae603a6_8df821ba",
        "filename": "android/bazel_handler.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 719,
      "author": {
        "id": 1903985
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-09-07T19:04:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks! I agree `encode_dict_value` is a misnomer - renaming to `encode_list_or_primitive`\n\n`encode_list` needs to call `encode_primitive` - so can\u0027t combine them into `encode_shallow_value` and involve self-recursion [aside: \"shallow\" doesn\u0027t sound right for a list]\n\nrant: I thought Starlark allowed recursion - prohibiting recursion to make a language non-Turing-Complete is usually not pragmatic.\n\nfyi: this is supposed to be a drop-in placeholder for json.encode(), which we should make available through a CL in bazel.",
      "parentUuid": "2b246cde_5bed469c",
      "revId": "1a1137d6aa1c447e35d3a0ee896c3275239f6225",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
